// Intentionally no include guard: consumers define CF_ROW and CF_STUB.
// CF_ROW(since, name, C return, wasm3 signature, pointer policy, parameter list).
// Parameters: (arity, (A/B, C type, name, 0), (PA/PB, pointer type, name, checked bytes), ...).
// A/PA are first arguments; B/PB are subsequent arguments.
// STRING95/127 validate the full guest range before truncation. SEQUENCE
// clamps count before validation. XBM rejects dimensions outside 1..128/1..64.
// CF_STUB(since, module, name, C return, signature, behavior, return policy, parameters)
// describes the same unpacking and memory checks for WASI/env stubs.
// The surface is add-only forever. New rows take since = the new CF_HAL_ABI.
// Breaking changes add a new import name; never change or remove an import.
CF_ROW(1, nop, int32_t, "i(i)", PLAIN, (1, (A, int32_t, x, 0)))
